ATH_0004> and\n<MATH_0005> are cofiltered diagrams in <MATH_0006>,\nthen we can define\n<MATH_0007>\nThere is a canonical functor <MATH_0008>\nwhich maps <MATH_0009> to the <TEXTITOPEN_0002>constant system<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> on <MATH_0010>. This is a fully\nfaithful embedding. In this language one sees that a diagram <MATH_0011> is\nessentially constant if and only if <MATH_0012> is isomorphic to a constant system.\nIf we ever need this material, then we will formulate this into a lemma\nand prove it here.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:319e76f1edaa7919f0f4b6236ad4419a941d2467e3bf92f027c21e16ce4e8cb1", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:05PX:remark/0001"}}}], "input_freeze": {"hash": "sha256:43193fdbba4118042ed46102d4748528c468194f0e76ca808d296541adfdaf54", "path": "translation-data/source-adoption-inputs/p0-52-algebraization-p041.json"}, "model_output": {"hash": "sha256:bad9dd51257172ef8d8ecc297592648376233c37d61a637b0f8e1d769be09d9f", "path": "docs/evidence/p0-52-algebraization-p041-raw-01.jsonl", "record_hash": "sha256:009f1d808f9b1bc3b74ab5993b53d04f38a52ac5f16f6f518f8d9a295b07626c"}, "neighbor_unit_ids": ["tag:0EIQ:proof"], "policy_revision": "git:c4895b2b9bf3fca2cca824ee70162f0c2033d93d", "prior_generations": [], "prompt_version": "translator-v2", "source_adoption_id": "p0-52-algebraization-p041", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "style_guide_path": "config/style-guide.md", "turn_id": "01a20b26-4e7a-7e12-a320-d5177dc7641c", "unit_id": "tag:0EIQ:statement"}, "context_hash": "sha256:1d810638dd22daaa30ec3014002c53a988cb1fa346fabcdafb76277e15b455fc", "created_at": "2026-11-24T01:23:11.907751+00:00", "glossary_revision": "git:c4895b2b9bf3fca2cca824ee70162f0c2033d93d", "harness_id": "codex", "harness_version": "0.171.0", "model_id": "gpt-6.1-sol", "model_identity_confidence": "declared", "model_lane": "openai-gpt-6.1-sol", "model_record_id": "openai:gpt-6.1-sol:declared", "model_snapshot": null, "notes": [], "prompt_version": "